{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/239421-ideas-and-questions-about-dragon-blooded-aspects","id":239421,"title":"Ideas And Questions About Dragon-Blooded Aspects","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-24T12:24:01-07:00","id":239421,"title":"Ideas And Questions About Dragon-Blooded Aspects","content":"Ok I think I got it<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_description\">HTML Code:</div> <pre class=\"bbcode_code notranslate\" style=\"max-height:calc(30 * 1.4rem + 2 * var(--bbcode-padding) + var(--h-scrollbar-allowance));\">Would you like to see DB whose elemental focus is shaped by the essence of their birthplace? For example an Earth Aspect from the South may have access to special charms that allow them to manipulate sand in unique ways, or a Fire Aspect from the volcanic islands in the West might have charms related to magma and sulfuric smoke. Likewise I could see Air Aspects with stronger affinity to lightning storms, Water Aspects who build and shape ice, and Wood Aspects who utilise fungi and spores. I think it would be cool if the specialised essence of a DBs home could help to shape the way their exaltation manifests, maybe even with slightly different Anima powers. Do you think all DB should be able to manipulate all five elements? I have always disliked having to cross over into charms very clearly flavoured as utilising a specific element that is not your base aspect. I find something really appealing about having that one element that is the embodiment of your character, and it bugs me when playing an Air Aspect if I have to take heavy obvious earth and fire charms to have any resistance or dodge ability. I think EX3 DB charms are going to include more that cross the last edition\ufffds aspect-ability boundaries, as well as more that feature multiple elemental sub-versions within the same charm. I think it would also be cool to see more charms that leave the elemental aspect and visual description up to the player, like a stealth charm that has a single mechanical effect but can conjure clouds of smoke, mist, sand, pollen, or buffeting winds, whatever the player feels suit their character.</pre> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","user":"turkeygiant","date":". 08-24-2014, 10:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T12:28:28-07:00","id":239440,"title":"","content":"Arrrrgh the forum keeps on cutting off my last two paragraphs!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T19:26:10-07:00","id":239796,"title":"","content":"Ok here is what I meant to post....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_description\">HTML Code:</div> <pre class=\"bbcode_code notranslate\" style=\"max-height:calc(30 * 1.4rem + 2 * var(--bbcode-padding) + var(--h-scrollbar-allowance));\">Would you like to see DB whose elemental focus is shaped by the essence of their birthplace? For example an Earth Aspect from the South may have access to special charms that allow them to manipulate sand in unique ways, or a Fire Aspect from the volcanic islands in the West might have charms related to magma and sulfuric smoke. Likewise I could see Air Aspects with stronger affinity to lightning storms, Water Aspects who build and shape ice, and Wood Aspects who utilise fungi and spores. I think it would be cool if the specialised essence of a DBs home could help to shape the way their exaltation manifests, maybe even with slightly different Anima powers. Do you think all DB should be able to manipulate all five elements? I have always disliked having to cross over into charms very clearly flavoured as utilising a specific element that is not your base aspect. I find something really appealing about having that one element that is the embodiment of your character, and it bugs me when playing an Air Aspect if I have to take heavy obvious earth and fire charms to have any resistance or dodge ability. I think EX3 DB charms are going to include more that cross the last edition\ufffds aspect-ability boundaries, as well as more that feature multiple elemental sub-versions within the same charm. I think it would also be cool to see more charms that leave the elemental aspect and visual description up to the player, like a stealth charm that has a single mechanical effect but can conjure clouds of smoke, mist, sand, pollen, or buffeting winds, whatever the player feels suit their character.</pre> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T19:36:22-07:00","id":239807,"title":"","content":"I'm of two minds on the multi-element association.<br /> <br /> <b>No</b><br /> I like the notion of elementally-aspected characters really digging into the themes of that element and seeing it interpreted and expressed in different ways. I enjoy it when a character's aspect isn't just window dressing but rather that it says something important and deep about who they are and how they relate to others and the world around them. I feel as though when you begin to allow characters to adopt other elements, at that point elements become costume. You put on a different hat because it's useful or it looks cool. In this vein I would like to say that I think there is something intriguing about the notion of a character who, through great trauma or enlightenment actually changes their aspect - leaving their birth aspect behind and being reborn in the element that reflects who they truly are on a fundamental level beyond that of mere apprehension and consciousness.<br /> <br /> <b>Yes</b><br /> I like the idea that the elements are not isolated and independent but are coterminous and work together to create and support life - that together they are stronger and have deeper meaning. I think there's something to be said of a character who learns what balance within him or herself and the world means and how cooperation isn't just something you do with other people. To that end, there is something dramatic and interesting about a character who begins to demonstrate two or more elemental aspects. When an Earth-Aspected Dynast who is over-burdened with familial duties and loyalties snaps and is forced to learn that in order to be balanced, sane and effective, you have to be prepared to let go of your identity and priorities and, as a result, begins to display Fire or Air or, if they pick up a &quot;go with the flow&quot; attitude about life, water. Or a character who has a traumatic near-death experience and learns the true value of life, suddenly displaying wood-aspected essence.<br /> <br /> This also creates room for interesting legends of Dragonblooded who learned mastery of all five elements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T21:33:26-07:00","id":239899,"title":"","content":"I sort of like how the restrictions on DBs make it hard to break from a stereotype, though still possible. So an air aspect who uses a lot of archery and dodge is a rarity but you can do it. It also helps, I think, to make them unique among exigents that might seem DB like. Like an exalt of a fire god might be powerfully skilled with archery, particularly fire wands, or something. Being a fire aspect DB you don't naturally have any special connections to archery or fire wands or anything, melee is fire's thing. Restrictions breed creativity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}